WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
Two glass tubes stand side
by side on the bench.

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.220
One is marked all the way up,
with a valve at the bottom.

3
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.780
It can deliver any volume you need.

4
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.200
The other has a bulb in the
middle and just one mark.

5
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.640
It delivers one fixed
volume, and nothing else.

6
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:20.300
So why would a chemist pick
the tube that can do less?

7
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.500
In this mission, you'll run
a titration step by step,

8
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.800
and make up a standard solution.

9
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.400
Then you'll match each
hazard to a control measure,

10
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.640
and find the step that lets a method down.

11
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:36.360
Your mission: explain why a chemist
would pick a tube with just one mark.